    "q-124492": {
      "dom_id": "step-q124492",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Which of the following is equivalent to $(n-2)!$ for any $n\\ge 4?$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the definition of factorial, we have\n\n$$\n(n-2)!=(n-2)\\cdot (n-3)\\cdot (n-4)\\cdot (n-5)\\cdot \\,⋯\\,\\cdot 2\\cdot 1.\n$$\n\nNow, applying the factorial definition to all but the first two factors, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(n-2)! & =(n-2)\\cdot (n-3)\\cdot \\overset{(n-4)!}{\\overset{⏞}{(n-4)\\cdot (n-5)\\cdot \\,⋯\\,\\cdot 2\\cdot 1}} \\\\  & =(n-2)\\cdot (n-3)\\cdot (n-4)!\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-124492-a",
              "type": "math",
              "value": "(n-2)\\cdot (n-3)",
