    "q-122060": {
      "dom_id": "step-q122060",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Given that $n\\ge 2$ is an integer, simplify $\\frac{(n-2)!(n+1)!}{(n!)^{2}}.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, notice the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n! & =n\\cdot (n-1)\\cdot (n-2)! \\\\ (n+1)! & =(n+1)\\cdot n!\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we cancel the $(n-2)!$ and $n!$ that occur in both the numerator and the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(n-2)!(n+1)!}{(n!)^{2}} & =\\frac{(n-2)!(n+1)!}{n!\\cdot n!} \\\\  & =\\frac{(n-2)!\\cdot (n+1)\\cdot n!}{n!\\cdot n\\cdot (n-1)\\cdot (n-2)!} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{(n-2)!}\\cdot (n+1)\\cdot \\cancel{n!}}{\\cancel{n!}\\cdot n\\cdot (n-1)\\cdot \\cancel{(n-2)!}} \\\\  & =\\frac{n+1}{n(n-1)}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
