    "q-122049": {
      "dom_id": "step-q122049",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Given that $n\\ge 0$ is an integer, simplify $\\frac{(n+3)!}{n!}.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, notice the following:\n\n$$\n(n+3)!=(n+3)\\cdot (n+2)\\cdot (n+1)\\cdot n!\n$$\n\nThen, we cancel the $n!$ that occurs in both the numerator and the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(n+3)!}{n!} & =\\frac{(n+3)\\cdot (n+2)\\cdot (n+1)\\cdot n!}{n!} \\\\  & =\\frac{(n+3)\\cdot (n+2)\\cdot (n+1)\\cdot \\cancel{n!}}{\\cancel{n!}} \\\\  & =(n+1)(n+2)(n+3)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
