    "q-79305": {
      "dom_id": "step-q79305",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "Given that $m\\ge 1$ is an integer, simplify $\\frac{(m+2)!}{(m+2)\\text{ }(m-1)!}=$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we notice that\n\n$$\n(m+2)!=(m+2)(m+1)(m)(m-1)!\n$$\n\nThen, we can cancel the $(m+2)$ and $(m-1)!$ that occur in both the numerator and the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(m+2)!}{(m+2)\\text{ }(m-1)!} & =\\frac{(m+2)\\cdot (m+1)\\cdot m\\cdot (m-1)!}{(m+2)\\cdot (m-1)!} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{(m+2)}\\cdot (m+1)\\cdot m\\cdot \\cancel{(m-1)!}}{\\cancel{(m+2)}\\cdot \\cancel{(m-1)!}} \\\\  & =(m+1)\\cdot m \\\\  & ={m}^{2}+m\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
